---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "types", label: "Input types" },
  { id: "inline", label: "Inline" },
  { id: "password-visibility", label: "Password visibility" },
  { id: "number-stepper", label: "Number stepper" },
  { id: "otp", label: "One-time code" },
  { id: "textarea", label: "Textarea" },
  { id: "file", label: "File input" },
  { id: "color", label: "Color" },
  { id: "character-counter", label: "Character counter" },
  { id: "api", label: "Form helpers API" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="text_inputs" sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          Wrap the control in a <code>.field</code>. The
          <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> after the control is the floating
          label. Mark an icon <code>prefix</code> or <code>suffix</code> to
          set its side, and make it <code>aria-hidden</code>. A
          <code>&lt;small&gt;</code> holds supporting text. The default is
          the M3 filled field. Add <code>outlined</code> for the outlined
          variant.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tokens follow the
          <a href="https://m3.material.io/components/text-fields/specs">M3 text field spec</a>.
          Height is 56dp. Filled is a <code>surface-container-highest</code> well with
          4dp top corners and a 1dp / 2dp bottom indicator. Outlined is a
          1dp / 2dp <code>outline</code> at 4dp. The label is
          <code>body-large</code> at rest and <code>body-small</code> floated.
          Input text is <code>body-large</code> / <code>on-surface</code>.
          Icons are 24dp, 12dp from the edge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Add <code>placeholder=" "</code> (one space) so the label floats
          with CSS only. A missing placeholder, or any other string, keeps
          the label floated. Importing the bundle runs
          <code>Forms.Init()</code>. It validates <code>.validate</code>
          fields on <code>change</code> and starts textareas and file paths.
          Character Counter is not in <code>AutoInit()</code>.
        </p>

        <form class="row">
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <input id="first_name" type="text" placeholder=" " maxlength="20" aria-describedby="first_name-help">
            <label for="first_name">First name</label>
            <small id="first_name-help">Supporting text</small>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field outlined">
            <input id="last_name" type="text" placeholder=" " maxlength="20">
            <label for="last_name">Last name</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <input id="disabled_filled" type="text" placeholder=" " value="I am not editable" disabled>
            <label for="disabled_filled">Disabled</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field outlined">
            <input id="disabled_outlined" type="text" placeholder=" " value="Not editable too" disabled>
            <label for="disabled_outlined">Disabled</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">place</span>
            <span class="material-symbols suffix" aria-hidden="true">gps_fixed</span>
            <input id="inp-location" type="text" placeholder=" " value="Planet Earth">
            <label for="inp-location">Location</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field outlined">
            <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">bubble_chart</span>
            <span class="material-symbols suffix" aria-hidden="true">error</span>
            <input id="inp-error" class="invalid" type="text" placeholder=" " value="$%/'#sdf" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="inp-error-help">
            <label for="inp-error">Failing input</label>
            <small id="inp-error-help">Invalid characters. Please use 0-9 only.</small>
          </div>
        </form>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <input id="first_name" type="text" placeholder=" " aria-describedby="first_name_help">
  <label for="first_name">First name</label>
  <small id="first_name_help">Supporting text</small>
</div>

<div class="field outlined">
  <input id="last_name" type="text" placeholder=" ">
  <label for="last_name">Last name</label>
</div>

<div class="field">
  <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">place</span>
  <span class="material-symbols suffix" aria-hidden="true">gps_fixed</span>
  <input id="loc" type="text" placeholder=" ">
  <label for="loc">Location</label>
</div>
`} />
        <p>
          Put <code>invalid</code> or <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> on the
          input for the error state. Do not put <code>error</code> on the
          wrapper. That class is a color utility and fills the field.
          <code>.supporting-text</code> and <code>.prefix</code> /
          <code>.suffix</code> remain as aliases.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.types}>
        <p>
          <code>email</code>, <code>password</code>, and the other native
          text-like types get the same styling. Add <code>validate</code> to
          check the value with HTML5 constraint validation on
          <code>change</code>. It toggles <code>invalid</code> and
          <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> on the input, so a screen reader
          hears the error state too.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also adds the field's <code>[data-error]</code> supporting text
          to the input's <code>aria-describedby</code>, so the error the CSS
          shows is read with the field. It gives that text an id if it has
          none and keeps the ids already there. There is no green
          <code>valid</code> style.
        </p>
        <form class="row">
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <input id="email" type="email" class="validate" placeholder=" " aria-describedby="email-help">
            <label for="email">Email</label>
            <small id="email-help" data-error="Enter a valid email">Supporting text</small>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <input id="password" type="password" class="validate" placeholder=" " maxlength="20">
            <label for="password">Password</label>
          </div>
        </form>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <input id="email" type="email" class="validate" placeholder=" " aria-describedby="email_help">
  <label for="email">Email</label>
  <small id="email_help" data-error="Enter a valid email">Supporting text</small>
</div>
`} />
        <p>
          <code>validate</code> also honors <code>data-length</code> and
          marks the field <code>invalid</code> when the value is longer than
          that number. Prefer <code>maxlength</code> when you want the
          browser to cap input.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.inline}>
        <p>Add <code>inline</code> to sit the field in a line of text.</p>
        <form>
          <p>
            This is an inline input field:
            <span class="field inline">
              <input id="email_inline" type="email" class="validate" placeholder=" ">
              <label for="email_inline">Email</label>
            </span>
          </p>
        </form>
<Code code={`
This is an inline input field:
<span class="field inline">
  <input id="email_inline" type="email" class="validate" placeholder=" ">
  <label for="email_inline">Email</label>
</span>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["password-visibility"]}>
        <p>
          A trailing <code>.icon-button</code> with <code>suffix</code> is a
          control in the field. It keeps its 40dp target and takes clicks.
          Give it <code>password-toggle</code>, two icons and
          <code>aria-pressed="false"</code>, and pressing it shows the
          password as text. The name stays "Show password", and
          <code>aria-pressed</code> says which way it is. Submitting or
          resetting the form hides the password again.
        </p>
        <div class="field" style="max-width: 20rem;">
          <input id="demo-password" type="password" placeholder=" " value="correct horse" autocomplete="off">
          <label for="demo-password">Password</label>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix password-toggle" aria-label="Show password" aria-pressed="false">
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">visibility</span>
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">visibility_off</span>
          </button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <input id="password" type="password" placeholder=" " autocomplete="current-password">
  <label for="password">Password</label>
  <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix password-toggle"
          aria-label="Show password" aria-pressed="false">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">visibility</span>
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">visibility_off</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["number-stepper"]}>
        <p>
          Add two trailing icon buttons with <code>data-step="down"</code> and
          <code>data-step="up"</code> to step a number input the way the arrow
          keys do, within its <code>min</code>, <code>max</code> and
          <code>step</code>. Name each button with what it changes. The Forms
          behavior does the stepping, and each press fires <code>input</code>
          and <code>change</code>. The browser's own spin buttons are hidden.
          A disabled, read-only or <code>step="any"</code> input is left alone.
        </p>
        <div class="field">
          <input id="demo-quantity" type="number" placeholder=" " value="1" min="1" max="10">
          <label for="demo-quantity">Quantity</label>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-step="down" aria-label="Decrease quantity">
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">remove</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-step="up" aria-label="Increase quantity">
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
          </button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <input id="quantity" type="number" placeholder=" " value="1" min="1" max="10">
  <label for="quantity">Quantity</label>
  <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-step="down" aria-label="Decrease quantity">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">remove</span>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="icon-button suffix" data-step="up" aria-label="Increase quantity">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.otp}>
        <p>
          <code>input.otp</code> draws one native input as a row of cells.
          Paste, autofill from <code>autocomplete="one-time-code"</code> and
          undo keep working, and a screen reader hears one field. Give it
          <code>inputmode="numeric"</code> and a <code>maxlength</code> equal
          to <code>--md-comp-otp-length</code> (6 by default). Label it
          outside any <code>.field</code>.
        </p>
        <label for="demo-code" class="body-medium">Verification code</label>
        <input id="demo-code" class="otp mb-3" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="one-time-code" maxlength="6" pattern="[0-9]{6}">
<Code code={`
<label for="code">Verification code</label>
<input id="code" class="otp" type="text" inputmode="numeric"
       autocomplete="one-time-code" maxlength="6" pattern="[0-9]{6}">
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.textarea}>
        <p>
          Use <code>textarea.expressive-textarea</code> inside
          <code>.field</code>. Textareas grow with their
          content. <code>Forms.Init()</code> starts every
          <code>.expressive-textarea</code> on <code>DOMContentLoaded</code>.
        </p>
        <form class="row">
          <div class="s12 field">
            <textarea id="textarea1" class="expressive-textarea" placeholder=" "></textarea>
            <label for="textarea1">Textarea</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 field">
            <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">mode_edit</span>
            <textarea id="textarea2" class="expressive-textarea" placeholder=" "></textarea>
            <label for="textarea2">Message</label>
          </div>
        </form>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <textarea id="textarea1" class="expressive-textarea" placeholder=" "></textarea>
  <label for="textarea1">Textarea</label>
</div>
`} />
        <p>If you add a textarea after load, initialize it yourself:</p>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Forms.InitTextarea(document.querySelector('#textarea1'));
`} />
        <p>
          Setting <code>.value</code> in script does not resize the field.
          Call <code>textareaAutoResize</code> afterwards.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.file}>
        <p>
          A <code>.file-field.field</code> pairs a button with a path field.
          <code>Forms.Init()</code> copies the chosen file name into
          <code>input.file-path</code>.
        </p>
        <form>
          <div class="file-field field">
            <label class="button">
              File
              <input type="file">
            </label>
            <div class="file-path-wrapper">
              <input class="file-path" type="text" placeholder=" " readonly aria-label="Selected file">
            </div>
          </div>
        </form>
<Code code={`
<div class="file-field field">
  <label class="button">
    File
    <input type="file">
  </label>
  <div class="file-path-wrapper">
    <input class="file-path" type="text" placeholder=" " readonly aria-label="Selected file">
  </div>
</div>
`} />
        <p>Add <code>multiple</code> to allow more than one file.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.color}>
        <p>
          An <code>&lt;input type="color"&gt;</code> keeps the browser's
          picker and shows as a 40px round swatch of the chosen color in a
          48px target. Label it like any field, and keep it outside a
          <code>.field</code>, which would give it the 56dp text well.
        </p>
        <p>
          <label for="demo-accent">Accent color</label>
          <input id="demo-accent" type="color" value="#c6a0f6">
        </p>
<Code code={`
<label for="accent">Accent color</label>
<input id="accent" type="color" value="#c6a0f6">
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["character-counter"]}>
        <p>
          Character Counter is not in <code>AutoInit()</code>. It reads
          <code>maxlength</code> (not <code>data-length</code>) and writes
          <code>current/max</code> into a <code>.character-counter</code>
          span. Overflow adds <code>invalid</code> on the field.
        </p>
        <form class="row">
          <div class="s12 m6 field">
            <input id="input_text_counter" type="text" maxlength="10" placeholder=" ">
            <label for="input_text_counter">Input text</label>
          </div>
          <div class="s12 field">
            <textarea id="textarea_counter" class="expressive-textarea" maxlength="120" placeholder=" "></textarea>
            <label for="textarea_counter">Textarea</label>
          </div>
        </form>
<Code code={`
Expressive.CharacterCounter.init(
  document.querySelectorAll('#input_text_counter, #textarea_counter')
);
`} />
        <p>Retrieve a counter with <code>Expressive.CharacterCounter.getInstance(input)</code>.
          Call <code>updateCounter()</code> after assigning the value from script, or dispatch
          <code>input</code>. Its <code>counterEl</code> is the generated polite live-region span;
          <code>isValidLength</code> reports whether the current length fits <code>maxlength</code>.
          <code>isInvalid</code> tracks the invalid styling state. <code>destroy()</code> removes the
          span and listeners. CharacterCounter has no configurable options.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.api}>
    <p>The root bundle calls <code>Forms.Init()</code>. With the modular entry, import
      <code>Forms</code> and call it once to install document behaviors and scan initial textareas
      and file-path inputs. Repeating <code>Forms.Init()</code> does not rescan new controls.</p>
    <table class="striped">
      <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>When to call it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>Forms.validateField(input)</code></td><td>After changing a validated field from script. Refreshes invalid styling and error descriptions. File inputs in a drop zone also refresh file validation and feedback. It does not submit the form.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Forms.InitTextarea(textarea)</code></td><td>Once for an <code>.expressive-textarea</code> inserted after the initial scan. Adds resize listeners and measures it when visible.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Forms.textareaAutoResize(textarea)</code></td><td>After assigning textarea text from script. A hidden textarea waits until it can be measured.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Forms.InitFileInputPath(input)</code></td><td>Once for a new file input inside <code>.file-field</code>. Copies chosen filenames into its <code>input.file-path</code> on change.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Forms.listDropZoneFiles(zone, input)</code></td><td>Rebuilds the zone's <code>.drop-zone-files</code> list from the file input, with localized file sizes. <code>validateField</code> also runs the relevant file feedback path.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <Code code={`const textarea = document.querySelector('textarea.expressive-textarea');
textarea.value = 'Updated from the application';
Expressive.Forms.textareaAutoResize(textarea);`} />
    <p><code>togglePassword(event)</code>, <code>stepNumber(event)</code>,
      <code>resetFormExtras(event)</code>, <code>summarizeErrors(event)</code>,
      <code>focusSummaryField(event)</code> and <code>markDropZone(event)</code> are event handlers
      installed by <code>Forms.Init()</code>. They handle password visibility, number steps,
      submit/reset cleanup, error summaries and drop feedback. Use their documented markup rather than
      calling these handlers manually. Forms has no per-field instance or <code>destroy()</code>.</p>
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
